# The NIGHT daypart is a midnight-crossing BAND in colloquial clock usage,
# not a uniform +12 PM shift: "la una de la nueche" is 01:00, "les diez de
# la nueche" is 22:00, twelve is midnight 00:00.  Small hours 1..5 stay AM,
# evening hours 6..11 are PM, twelve is midnight (band-split in resolver
# _clock_hms).  AST is Ibero-Romance and shares the same madrugada band
# [00:00, 06:00) as es/ca/pt (chronologia/dayparts.py); the 5|6 cut is
# inherited from the RAE/DIEC/Priberam-cited boundary for the sibling
# Ibero-Romance locales (see chronologia/locale/es/clock_meridiem_night.voc)
# pending native confirmation for Asturian (tracked in issue #266).
nueche
